# Debian packaging for git-nest (STUB -- not yet wired into the release
# workflow; see temp-doc/external-setup-guide.md for the external setup).
#
# When enabled, the release workflow builds a .deb from the assembled
# tarball and publishes it to a Launchpad PPA or a self-hosted APT repo.

Source: git-nest
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Flemming Steffensen <fsteff@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.0
Homepage: https://github.com/f-steff/git-nest

Package: git-nest
Architecture: all
Depends: git, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Manage many independent Git repositories as one cohesive project
 git-nest records and restores reproducible workspaces made from
 independent Git repositories, without submodules or monorepo pain.
